config AUDIO_ENABLE
    bool "Enable onboard audio (ES8311 codec + speaker test tone)"
    default y
    help
        Stage 1 of audio support: initializes the ES8311 codec and its I2S
        TX path at startup, and backs the debug-only POST /beep route with
        a short test tone. A beep/alarm capability is a legitimate native
        feature, so this defaults on - but audio is still an optional
        module, not part of the native firmware: the display, clock,
        sensors, battery, portal, and OTA all build and behave identically
        with this on or off.

        Turning this off removes the ES8311/I2S code and the
        espressif/esp_codec_dev managed dependency from the build entirely
        - audio_init() and audio_play_tone() become inline no-ops (see
        audio.hpp) rather than a runtime check, so none of this component
        ends up in the binary.
